  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1121 AM MDT Mon Jul 6 2026\n\nModels in good agreement through 7 days with the pattern\ndeveloping across the Western US.  Currently we have a ridge over\nthe Four Corners states that will be getting flattened and \nretrograde off into the eastern Pacific. Initially we will get \nsome drier air moving into eastern zones as NE flow develops. \nLooks like the Gila will have daily scattered storms with outflows\nhelping isolated storms develop over the lowlands Tue-Thu. As we \ngo into Fri and the weekend, the ridge will reestablish over CO/WY\nand this allows for a deeper ESE lower level flow to bring in \nsome Gulf moisture and storm chances return for the entire area.\nThis is even supported by the GFS and ECMWF ensemble means at Day\n7, so high confidence in this playing out as depicted in the\ndeterministic models. \n\nWith this shifting ridge, the drier air early in the period will\nallow temperatures to warm up back into the 100-105 range for most\nof the lowlands. NBM and especially MET temps seemed low and did\nraise up closer to the MAV. At this time, do not think Heat\nAdvisories will be necessary, but some areas of the lower RGV\ncould get to 105.",
